
==========================================================================
  ABSTRACT QSWITCH E2E DEMO (Linear DSL)
==========================================================================

Full pipeline: OCaml Linear DSL -> Bridge -> Python compile -> Circuit


==========================================================================
  PART 1: QSwitch Type Structure
==========================================================================

QSwitch[f, g] : Bool ⊗ Q → Bool ⊗ Q

where Bool = I + I (the 2-element sum type)

Structure:
  dist_l    : (I+I) ⊗ Q → (I⊗Q) + (I⊗Q)    [distribute]
  omap0     : Apply f⊕g bifunctorially       [branch operations]
  undist_l  : (I⊗Q) + (I⊗Q) → (I+I) ⊗ Q    [undistribute]

This is PURELY LINEAR DSL - no Bridge term hacking!


==========================================================================
  PART 2: QSwitch[H, S] - Full Linear DSL Construction
==========================================================================

QSwitch[H, S] semantics:
  |0⟩ ⊗ |ψ⟩ → |0⟩ ⊗ H(S(|ψ⟩))   (apply S then H)
  |1⟩ ⊗ |ψ⟩ → |1⟩ ⊗ S(H(|ψ⟩))   (apply H then S)

Emitting to Bridge term...

Bridge JSON:
{"node": "Seq", "f": {"node": "DistL", "a": {"node": "Unit"}, "b": {"node": "Unit"}, "c": {"node": "Q"}}, "g": {"node": "Seq", "f": {"node": "PlusMap", "ty_left": {"node": "Ten", "left": {"node": "Unit"}, "right": {"node": "Q"}}, "ty_right": {"node": "Ten", "left": {"node": "Unit"}, "right": {"node": "Q"}}, "left": {"node": "TenTerm", "f": {"node": "Id", "ty": {"node": "Unit"}}, "g": {"node": "Seq", "f": {"node": "S", "i": 0}, "g": {"node": "H", "i": 0}}}, "right": {"node": "TenTerm", "f": {"node": "Id", "ty": {"node": "Unit"}}, "g": {"node": "Seq", "f": {"node": "H", "i": 0}, "g": {"node": "S", "i": 0}}}}, "g": {"node": "UndistL", "a": {"node": "Unit"}, "b": {"node": "Unit"}, "c": {"node": "Q"}}}}

Compiling via Python backend...

2 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CS q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CS q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

✓ Compilation SUCCESS!

