==========================================================================
  PART 4: Linear DSL Components
==========================================================================

Showing that each component is a proper Linear DSL term:

dist_l one one q:
  {"node": "DistL", "a": {"node": "Unit"}, "b": {"node": "Unit"}, "c": {"node": "Q"}}

undist_l one one q:
  {"node": "UndistL", "a": {"node": "Unit"}, "b": {"node": "Unit"}, "c": {"node": "Q"}}

par0 (id one) gate_h:
  {"node": "TenTerm", "f": {"node": "Id", "ty": {"node": "Unit"}}, "g": {"node": "H", "i": 0}}

omap0 iq iq (id_I⊗H) (id_I⊗S):
  {"node": "PlusMap", "ty_left": {"node": "Ten", "left": {"node": "Unit"}, "right": {"node": "Q"}}, "ty_right": {"node": "Ten", "left": {"node": "Unit"}, "right": {"node": "Q"}}, "left": {"node": "TenTerm", "f": {"node": "Id", "ty": {"node": "Unit"}}, "g": {"node": "H", "i": 0}}, "right": {"node": "TenTerm", "f": {"node": "Id", "ty": {"node": "Unit"}}, "g": {"node": "S", "i": 0}}}


==========================================================================
  PART 5: Composing QSwitch Operations
==========================================================================

QSwitch composes because it's a proper morphism Bool⊗Q → Bool⊗Q:

QSwitch[H,S] ; QSwitch[X,Z]:
2 qubits, 12 gates
  X q[0]
  CS q[0, 1]
  CH q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CH q[0, 1]
  CS q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  CX q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 1]
  CZ q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

==========================================================================
  SUMMARY
==========================================================================

This demo shows PROPER Linear DSL usage for QSwitch:

1. TYPE-SAFE CONSTRUCTION
   - qswitch : (Q→Q) → (Q→Q) → (Bool⊗Q → Bool⊗Q)
   - GADT-enforced linearity

2. STRUCTURAL ISOMORPHISMS
   - dist_l  : (A+B) ⊗ C → (A⊗C) + (B⊗C)
   - undist_l: (A⊗C) + (B⊗C) → (A+B) ⊗ C
   - Proper inverses!

3. BIFUNCTORIAL ACTION
   - omap0 : (A→C) → (B→D) → ((A+B) → (C+D))
   - Applies different operations per branch

4. COMPOSITIONALITY
   - QSwitch[f,g] ; QSwitch[h,k] composes naturally
   - Types ensure correctness

NO Bridge term hacking - this is the REAL Linear DSL!


